{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And the one thousand seven hundred etc.</b> Meaning, the remainder. And our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Shemot Rabbah 51:5) that he forgot them, and when he remembered them he said ״וְאֶת הָאֶלֶף״ etc. — they are from what he made into hooks etc." "Now, according to those among the scholars (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 25:3) who hold that there was no silver in the donation of the Tabernacle apart from the half-shekel, the verse's saying <b>and the one thousand</b> is explained as follows: since we find that HaShem commanded regarding the silver donation a half-shekel, and in all the work of the Tabernacle we do not find that HaShem commanded the making of silver apart from the sockets and the hooks and their bands, and regarding the sockets He explained that a talent is needed per socket, but regarding the hooks HaShem did not inform their measure nor the measure of their bands — therefore Betzalel acted wisely and apportioned the remainder from the sockets and made them into hooks. For even though HaShem did not command their measure, from the fact that He gave a measure for the sockets, he understood that the hooks and their bands would come from the remainder. And therefore it says <b>and the one thousand</b> etc. <b>he made hooks</b> — meaning that he apportioned the amount for the hooks. And so too, if there had remained more or less, he would have apportioned the remainder. And if the verse had said ״וַיַּעַשׂ וָוִין״ etc., it would have been understood that this measure was stated from the mouth of El Elyon, but that is not so; rather, from the implication of the matter he understood, as mentioned." "And my opinion is not like this view, for certainly there was other silver in the donation of the Tabernacle besides the bekah per head, since the verse speaks fully in Vayakhel (Exodus 35:24): ״כָּל מֵרִים תְּרוּמַת כֶּסֶף וּנְחֹשֶׁת״ — and in this verse the words of Rabbi Abraham Ibn Ezra would not hold up as he sits on the verse (Exodus 25:3) ״וְזֹאת הַתְּרוּמָה״, and the discerning one will understand. Rather, the verse's saying <b>and the one thousand</b> is to be explained along the lines of what we explained on the verse (Exodus 38:24) ״כָּל הַזָּהָב״ etc. — meaning, that nothing was lost through the process of smelting and the details of the work; that even though he performed many details of work in the making of many hooks and their bands, nevertheless the number itself remained whole in the hooks and nothing was lost from it at all. This is what it means by <b>and the one thousand</b> etc. <b>he made hooks</b>. Take note."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:17.752302647Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}